# {{.project_name}}

Standalone evaluation project generated from the AAI platform template
(`evaluation-project`): curated datasets, reusable scorers, pinned
baselines, a two-tier CI gate, and published results.

## Local setup

Before generation, complete the platform's developer onboarding checklist.
Then run the generated preflight and setup:

```bash
python3.12 scripts/setup_dev.py
make check
```

Run `make help` for individual development, evaluation, and bundle targets.

Use `python3.12 scripts/setup_dev.py --check-only` to verify tools,
authentication, SDK volume access, and compute-policy visibility without
installing anything. The setup never grants permissions or creates cloud
resources.

## How this project evaluates

- **Datasets** — `evals/data/golden_cases.json` is the reviewed regression
  suite (gates releases; grow it toward 150+ cases and convert every
  production failure into a case). `edge_cases.json` is the capability suite
  (deliberately hard; report-only). `answer_sheet.json` holds recorded
  answers so scoring works without calling the application.
  `scripts/sync_dataset.py` publishes cases to the governed UC dataset
  `{{.catalog}}.{{.schema}}.{{.dataset_name}}`.
- **Scorers** — `src/app/scorers.py` holds deterministic code scorers (pure
  functions, unit-tested, run in both tiers). `src/app/judges.py` routes the
  Correctness/Safety judges and the executable `domain_policy` MLflow
  `Guidelines` scorer through the gateway-fronted `judge-model` endpoint.
  Align judges against explicitly sourced HUMAN labels first; the alignment
  notebook demonstrates a calibration/validation split and keeps experimental
  MemAlign disabled unless its extra dependencies and approved models are
  deliberately provided (`notebooks/01_align_judge.py`).
- **Gate** — thresholds live in `evals/gate_config.json`. Tier 1
  (`evals/offline_checks.py`, PR CI) applies the code-scorer thresholds to
  the answer sheet, verifies every gate category, and prevents report-only
  judges from becoming thresholds accidentally. Tier 2
  (`evals/evaluate.py`, credentialed) runs code scorers + judges, enforces
  every threshold plus regression against `evals/baseline.json`, and publishes
  a markdown report to the CI step summary. `domain_policy` runs report-only
  until held-out human calibration justifies moving it into `judge_metrics`
  with a threshold. Failure triage prints bounded row/scorer identifiers by
  default. `--show-triage-details` adds rationale/error text only when CI logs
  are approved for the evaluation data classification; those details can
  quote source content. After a released run passes: `--update-baseline`.
- **Targets** — score recorded answers (default) or a live endpoint:
  `python evals/evaluate.py --mode endpoint` (configure `target-model` in
  `aai-platform.yml`).

Deploy the scheduled suite with `databricks bundle validate -t dev` and
`databricks bundle deploy -t dev` (uncomment the cron block in
`resources/evaluation_job.yml` for continuous evaluation).

The platform team must onboard this repository (main-branch federated
credential, service principal, constrained compute, non-secret repository
variables) before the deploy workflow is enabled.
